def kth_smallest(arr, k):
    if len(arr) <= 1:
        return arr[0]

    # Create a min heap using the first element as the root
    heap = [arr[0]]
    i = 1

    while i < len(arr):
        # Add the next element to the heap if it's smaller than the root
        if arr[i] < heap[0]:
            heap.append(arr[i])
            i += 1
        else:
            i += 1

    # Extract the kth smallest element from the min heap
    return heap[k]
```

This function first initializes a min heap with the first element of the input array. Then, it iterates through the rest of the array and adds elements to the min heap if they are smaller than the current root. Finally, it extracts the kth smallest element from the min heap.

The time complexity of this algorithm is O(nlogn), as building and maintaining a min heap has a time complexity of O(nlogn). The space complexity is O(1), since the only variable used in the function is an array to store the elements of the min heap.

